# Testing, the command line and Rails

From the README of stationery <%= version %>. Online: <%= docs("testing") %>, <%= docs("cli") %> and <%= docs("rails") %>.

What a spec cannot see is checked by hand, with the pictures (`stationery render FILE --png`):
look at every page, count them (content that does not fit goes to another page without a
warning), and decode every barcode with `zbarimg -q FILE-1.png` (`brew install zbar`). A spec
can decode too, when zbar is installed:

```ruby
it "prints a Code 128 that scans" do
  label.to_png("tmp/label.png", monochrome: true)
  expect(`zbarimg -q tmp/label.png`).to include("CODE-128:SX0042771903")
end
```

